Clock-domain notes for the counter subsystem.

## `basic_counter.sv`

- `clk`, `high_low`, `addr`, `result` - control/readout side
- `d_clk`, `d`, `d_reset`, `d_valid`, `d_latch` - sampled data side
- `overflow` - latched overflow indication

## `counter_if.sv`

- `clk` - Avalon-MM programming and result-readout domain
- `d_clk` - live counter update domain for sampled signal statistics
- `reset_all` and `latch_all` are generated in `clk` and synchronized into `d_clk`
- selector updates cross from `clk` into `d_clk` through a coherent latest-value CDC update
- selected channels `d0`, `d1`, `d2` are derived from the registered copy of `d` using the `d_clk` selector copy

## Time-counter path

`time_counter.sv` is different from the other instruments:

- start/stop events are derived from selected channels in `counter_if.sv`
- elapsed time is measured in `clk`
- `ready` is reported back on the Avalon side as a latched status bit

